Trace — App Icon Source Set
====================================

This directory holds the source PNGs that `iconutil` consumes when producing
`AppIcon.icns`. The canonical icon files are:

    icon_16x16.png
    icon_16x16@2x.png
    icon_32x32.png
    icon_32x32@2x.png
    icon_128x128.png
    icon_128x128@2x.png
    icon_256x256.png
    icon_256x256@2x.png
    icon_512x512.png
    icon_512x512@2x.png

Run `scripts/make-icns.sh` after replacing these PNGs. The script renders
a placeholder set on-the-fly when none of the above files exist, so the
release pipeline is unblocked even without a designed icon. Replace the
placeholders with the real assets before any external release.

The placeholder uses `sips` and `tiffutil` shipped with macOS to render
a flat brand tile (no logo, no text, no emoji) from the AppShell visual
identity palette declared in spec §6.5.
